editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-13.md:145:*Registry seat, Ostrand. Records support, junior chair. Rotation: the seat's Fifth-days, until relieved.* There was nothing else. There never was. A rotation sheet told you where to sit and for how long. It did not tell you why, and in all his years of rotation sheets Havel had never once expected it to.
