editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-79-## 3. Expansion plan — where the ≈176,000 new words come from
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-80-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-81-Source ≈124,000 words retold at roughly equal weight, plus ≈176,000 of new room. Every item below serves the book promise ("the mid-tier academy as a real place with real stakes and real politics") or the arc (*I know what I can do* → *I need to understand why the system doesn't want me to be able to do it*). None changes an end state or opens a reserved truth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-82-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md:83:1. **The five-person cutaway system (+26k).** Source windows total about 13k (Seln ×5, Vastin ×2, Ilsev and Havel ×1 each). These grow to ≈39.8k across Seln, Lira, Vastin, Ilsev and Havel (see §5). *Why:* the formula's ~13% secondary share, and the book is about watchers. Each window shows a different grade of attention.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-84-2. **Lira's Copper season on the page (+18k).** The practice record (one developed bout); the climb rounds summarized as "six perfect afternoons" (two on the page, the rest compressed); round 7 against the Shield veteran (≈2k); round 8 against the cohort's Lira plan; the Fiske seeding bout at full length (≈3k); and the **Fiske semifinal**, which the source summarizes as "four exchanges again — harder ones, and one very long minute," staged as a developed fight from Lira's POV (≈3k). *Why:* the title object has to be earned in front of the reader, and the semifinal is the hip injury the final runs on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-85-3. **Brom's Rooke curriculum (+12k).** His first cohort hour on the page; Ephram's false feeds learned from the gallery as a learning fight; the "worse for a season" sessions; the nineteen exercises counted by Karis (14 at M5, through to the final); Merrick and Tarn developed; the repair seeded so the final's reveal is fair. *Why:* the final is decided by a repair that worked, and the reader must watch it being built.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-86-4. **Cael's pre-acquisition learning arcs (+17k).** Triage, built after a failure; the Lattice null as a full learning encounter with the Lattice instructor and a pupil; the sprung-floor re-audit of every ceiling in the log; Compression drills; the counter-study of Seln developed as Path theory step by step (glance instrument, failed maps, overlay, tests, the tax rate, the fatigue curve, the discarded column). *Why:* front-loaded teaching (formula §4), and so the reader can price the sixth fragment before it arrives.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-87-5. **The final Greyvane term on the page (+14k).** Karis's week-three find and her eleven-week attempt to kill it; the first Bracken letters; the Edran rematch as a developed learning fight (≈2.5k: Glass Path half-beat recovery, one exchange over his rate, the hip); Quenna's one sentence; Prynn at the gate; the road. *Why:* it puts the inter-book skip on the page and hands the movement a fight in its first hour.
--
