editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-265-- Ch13: Seln: "a position is an argument about where attention will go." · Log: "Sixth fragment. Bronze — the notice finally said a tier out loud, like the architecture decided I'd earned a number. Acquired from a man who doesn't know, in defense of a file with my name on it, during an operation he let me watch. I drew the line in advance and I stayed on my side of it. It cost anyway. Write that down too." · "A system that confirms you is a system that was listening."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-266-- Ch14: Lira: "I asked Hesk. In a letter. A year ago… You people treat information like it's rationed." · Brom: "You've spent two years learning to be the most awake person in every room. Now you own a thing that only works when you're furniture. You're going to hate this for about a year and then you're going to be very good at it." · Karis's chart: the fourth column reads *see holder*. · Log [coordinator 2026-10-05: "nine weeks" → "seventeen days" — the closed M4 calendar (Fiske's protected "Six weeks. I'll see you in the final.") and the final-on-the-19th / evaluation-on-the-20th plan fix the interval; see OWNER-DECISIONS #35]: "Sixteen. Six fragments. The Compact's best watcher watching out for me instead, and no way to thank him for it that wouldn't burn him. Semester evaluation in seventeen days. Whatever the system sends to watch it — we're ready. We built ready." · Anomaly: "Still open. Still real. Patience."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-267-- Ch15: Withrow: "The inspection is ordinary. His presence is the message. Somebody very high wants their own eyes on this, and they have sent the best pair they have." · Gault: "It is not good or bad. It is the mandate." · Bracken: "An argument persuades a person. A file survives a person leaving the room." · Log: "Last time the Compact came to an academy for me, they sent a warden with a challenge. This time they're sending an Archmarshal with no stated business at all. Coss I could read in a week. I don't know what reads an Archmarshal."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-268-- Ch16: Brom: "I've been trying to solve her for two years. Now I get faculty supervision and a crowd." · Bracken: "a thing that goes on being true in a room where nobody who built it is standing." · Log: "New opponent. No tells. Begin."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md:269:- Ch17: Vastin: *Observer product is testimony about the observer.* / *an evaluation that begins from its conclusion is a report about the evaluator.* · Marginalia: *Why concede the category?* / *Who taught him the schedule's structure?* / *Verify: three weeks' preparation — from what baseline?* · Log: "Coss enforced… Havel complied… Seln operates… This one evaluates… The Compact finally sent someone who takes notes the way I take notes."
