editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-300-## 12. Canon conflicts found in the source (for owner ruling; drafting proceeds on the recommendation unless the owner rules otherwise)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-301-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-302-- **C1 · Bracken's gender.** *She* in Ch1–3 (also Withrow in Ch2) and *he* from Ch13 onward, as in B5 Ch1, B6 and B7 Ch9. **Recommend he.** Do not rename (edition brief).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-303-- **C2 · Vastin's age.** Source Ch17, Ch21 and Ch23: "He was sixty now" / "a man of sixty." The Universe Bible says **51 at Book 4**, and Book 8's drafted prose says 53. **Recommend 51**, or no stated age. "Forty years" can stand as his own rounding (Book 8 treats it so).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md:304:- **C3 · Elapsed time since Kindling.** "Four years" (Havel Ch18; Vastin Ch23; Cael Ch24) and "since he was twelve" (Ch9; Seln Ch12) against the LOCKED Kindling at fourteen, which puts Book 4 about two years after it. Books 5–6 echo "four years," so this is series-wide drift. **Owner call.** Plan: "since his Kindling," "two years," or no count.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-305-- **C4 · Fiske's age.** Twenty (Ch3) vs "about nineteen" (Ch8, Cael's estimate). **Recommend twenty.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-306-- **C5 · Field-assessment unit length.** Announced as "Four sessions" (Ch12); later "Sixteen sessions. Thirty-two hours" (Ch23). **Recommend** a weekly unit across the term's back half (sixteen sessions), offered at the counter as "a unit for the back half of term." Owner call.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-307-- **C6 · Lira's season record.** Ch19 reads "Six wins, no losses," but the page shows more wins (rounds 7–8, Fiske twice). **Recommend** the true count, written at the ceremony.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/BOOK_MAP.md-308-- **C7 · Knowledge leak.** Hesk's "wrote 'keep looking'" and Cael's closing "wrote that I'm not an error" refer to a private Compact file note with no in-story channel. **Recommend** keeping both lines verbatim, framed as *inference*: Hesk's guess; Cael's belief from the renewal and the unchanged rotation. Owner call on whether to touch the wording.
--
