editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-21-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-22-- **The notice read in the records hall.** Nine at the table, and "anybody named in a scope reads the scope." The counsel's three deltas. The name and the room's reactions. Withrow on what an Archmarshal is: "The inspection is ordinary. His presence is the message…" Gault: "My wing changes nothing… It is not good or bad. It is the mandate."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-23-- **Rooke's correction in the covered walk:** half of his prediction was right; the other half was his to fix and he didn't. He sends the supervision stacks to Bracken that night. "Keep doing that… exactly as boring as it sounds." Cael revises Rooke's page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-24-- **The documentary defense, eleven days, as craft.** Certified copies; a second independent repeal search by a clerk who never saw Karis's notes; the forty-one-page directive tabbed; the numbered index. **"An argument persuades a person. A file survives a person leaving the room."** Karis: "If I fell down the bluff tomorrow, the enrollment would hold." Bracken to Cael: "Give me a dull month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:25:- **Delegation pages.** Nine of eleven from the library: counsel, clerks, escort; **Havel** ("he keeps rising and he keeps ending up wherever I am"); **Ilsev**'s six findings. The eleventh returns nothing: "This is the first time the archive has nothing and I am going to have to do it from the floor."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-26-- **The temperature week.** The rumor that another academy requested it; the suspension question at Bracken's counter; a first-year doing arithmetic on him. **Withrow's eleven-minute address:** "A performance is the only thing an inspection is actually able to detect… Least of all a sixteen-year-old." **Ephram on the stair:** the terms changed in Cael's favor, "anybody can look good in an empty room."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-27-- **Seln (cutaway, Ch41, ≈800):** the requisition; six filings laid side by side and read as an auditor would. "Complete, consistent, and containing nothing." Ilsev's findings read on the road up from his last posting. He adds nothing and removes nothing. **"What he kept, he kept."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-28-- **The schedule beside the final.** Copper final on the nineteenth of Reaping; observation reserved for the twentieth; the overlapping week. The rhyme with the Greyvane notice board. Log: "Coss I could read in a week…" and three men giving one instruction: hold the ordinary.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-29-- **The final settles (new on the page).** **Lira vs Fiske, semifinal (Lira window ≈2,000 of a ≈3,000 fight):** four exchanges again, harder, and "one very long minute at the end that the first meeting had not needed." This is where the leading hip is damaged; the final runs on it. Fiske's knowledge of Lira is now complete, and Lira must win with less. One brief Fiske–Lira exchange after, with nothing said that reveals the future. **Brom vs Merrick (≈1,200)**, taken in the fifth. "Right." / "You're going to be unbearable about this." / "Now I get faculty supervision and a crowd." Karis: "It's the nineteenth."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-30-- **No sparring for nine days.** Lira racks the batons: "I've beaten you nine times in two years and you've beaten me eleven… neither of us fights chess." Cael's sentence: "two Iron-equivalent practitioners who have never been allowed to fight anybody their own size." "Nine days. Nobody talks about hips."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-31-- **The three columns** (growth / control / five things), and the moment hiding and honesty become the same operation. Then the **idle-state slip in hall three** with a wing observer at the rail. Brom: "You went." In the corridor: "How far." / "What do you think a three-hour evaluation is?" The plan is rebuilt with holding as the *first* task: "a bout with a stranger where the stranger is me."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-32-- **Bracken closes the file:** four boxes, 311 documents, "a thing that goes on being true in a room where nobody who built it is standing." The institution holds still for three days, "the hardest athletic feat he had seen all season."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:33:- **Arrival, the twelfth of Reaping. Havel window (≈2,400):** up the bluff road in the second carriage; the courtyard corners before its center; deciding where the subject would stand and not looking up there; his career's two rises; nothing above his clearance. Then Cael on the upper tier: Ilsev carries her own case. **The third carriage.** The count comes back wrong three ways: the aides orbit; the man generates no orbit; the insignia announces an altitude the bearing never performs. Attention sampled *evenly* on purpose. "That one crossed a courtyard." **"New opponent. No tells. Begin."**
