editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-19-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-20-Introduce the evaluator as the book's antagonist keynote, legitimate and competent, with nothing villainous. Show the institution's paper hold under scrutiny. Ask the arc's sharpest question once and pocket it. Turns and promises:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-21-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-22-- **Vastin (cutaway, Ch45):** the transcript's fourth reading in the panel's order. "Observer product is testimony about the observer." The six-sheet monitoring appendix read in nine minutes and not annotated: a fact about the officer's *position*. Two thousand margins, six conclusions. The three marginal questions. The gap: "three weeks… from what baseline?" The maxim learned at twenty-three, understood four years later in a bad month. **Age per C2** (default: show his hand's winter stiffness and do not state a number). "He had filed no question."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:23:- **An inspection is furniture moving.** Closed doors, boxes; the senior clerk's bad knee tells the working order; counsel's talking and reading "use different rooms in her head." **Havel's inch** in the covered walk (Havel ≈800 from his side: what decency his instructions permit).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-24-- **The facility review in hall three.** He made the deliberate choice to change nothing and slept nine hours. Brom drives a three-quarter redirect drill. Cael **runs it on structure instead of the read** because the read at depth and the idle state share one account. Fifty-four clean of sixty. Brom: "Read's off." / "On purpose." / "Then it's the right kind of off." The ledger reads "It is not a capability. It is rent," and "Fifty minutes cost me the read. The twentieth is three hours." Seven at the rail; one never moves. **Ilsev window (≈1,500):** her four questions about the observer's recording protocol, none about the enrollee.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-25-- **The placement bout.** He arrives at the second exchange and leaves in the fourth, before the result. Cael's hour of working it out: he came for the *panel's thresholds*. "Exactly what I would have done." **Gault's three questions**, all about the resistance posts' calibration interval: "This one started with the ruler."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26:- **Two men.** The compiled case's receipt stamp, seen upside down: read and unmarked. "The whole of it rests on a man I cannot read." The taxonomy on the empty upper tier while porters sweep: "Coss enforced. Havel complied. Seln operates. This one evaluates… The Compact finally sent someone who takes notes the way I take notes."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-27-- **The charter session (≈5,000 across two chapters).** Cael sits against the wall, placed where the room will notice him least. Provenance: two certified schedules four hundred miles apart; the collation sheet. Counsel goes quiet for ninety seconds: "It's good." Then supersession by implication, a genuinely strong argument. **Withrow answers it herself**: article forty-one's repeal list of eleven clauses; the transitional article on converting *existing assay enrollments* ("You do not draft a conversion procedure for a thing you consider a dead letter").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:28:- **Ilsev (cutaway, Ch49):** the return sheet; fourteen months; "a marking cannot be older than the paper"; "Either the answer is a routing failure, or the answer is not an answer"; the thought she does not permit; the second referral in eleven minutes with its grounds sentence; cold tea. **Havel (cutaway):** logging the tray; the notebook with four pages of ninety; the fourth entry; the one line that breaks his rule (**C3: use the owner's figure; default "Two years. Two of us now. Nothing has ever come back with a name on it."**).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-29-- **The afternoon.** Ilsev makes the operative sentence be read twice, subordinate clause first. To Gault: is this the clause's evaluation, or one named after it? Gault: "It tells me to set one, apply it, and write it down. I have. I do. I will." To counsel: unlawful or irregular? "Irregular." **The finding, verbatim.** Vastin's pen moves five times, only on procedure: "He is calibrating the instrument. I am the reading."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-30-- **The drift in the gaps.** Nine hours in a chair is worse than a floor: twice, then once badly, the folder set on the empty chair beside him. **Karis's foot finds his ankle** under the table. "It is a friend, which is worth more and works less often."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-31-- **The back room, re-shelving.** Karis's handwriting went sideways at the transitional article. The terminology article "four articles from" the conversion article, in one instrument. **[UNBOUND] said once** ("One hand took a word that meant [UNBOUND] and wrote *shattered* over it…"), then closed: "a coincidence with good posture." **"Why retire a working method?"** Cael's log: confused systems ask; this one renames and closes doors. "I don't need to know who. I need to know why it's built this way." "Four days to the final. Five to the twentieth."
