editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md-19-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md-20-The watcher is found, then studied, and the season opens on the cage. Turns and promises:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md-21-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md-22-- **The count that broke**, from bookkeeping rather than suspicion: TA 0 of 7, then 0 of 31 against an expected five. "That was not an unlikely draw. That was a man doing something." The **four failed maps**, each kept and written down as discarded ("killed, no signal"). The fifth map is gridded by *lines*, and the question becomes **"Where would I stand?"** Nineteen of nineteen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:23:- **Tests.** The paper-swap test is useless and he says so. Forty minutes early in hall three: the gallery is empty and the man walks on — **"He needs a crowd."** The brass session-lamp reflection, twice. **"Avoidance at that precision is aim."** Three grades of monitoring: Havel, the rotations, this.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md-24-- **The council.** Lira wants Withrow told. Karis: "an instrument you can read for an instrument you can't find." Brom: "We know where their eyes are." "It's not settled, it's *outvoted*." Three agreements: no confrontation (report breaks); the boring truth; he studies him. "That is the meanest thing you've ever said." / "accounting with a *tone*." The price: the read degrades because counting spends the same fuel.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md-25-- **Seln (cutaway, Ch18).** Observation, not inference; the colleague ended by one adjective. The first product, true and dry, walked down to the Ostrand courier himself. Gault's four questions. The arithmetic error that settles the office's opinion of him. **Made on day twenty-three** at the empty gallery, and the eleven seconds of being pleased before the thought finished. Made twice before in fifteen years, never by a target. Withdraw, escalate, or keep working: he keeps working. The subject does nothing, and Seln feels *accounted for*. "The interesting question is who taught him to watch."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md-26-- **Path theory from outside.** No declaration, then a declaration *smeared across four hours*. He measures it through other people's eyes: about a third less attention lands at the rail when the man stands there. It is a tax, a rate, so it must be a resource with a curve. The **fatigue curve** shows the positions degrade after about four hours. The "Discarded / cannot reach" column: range, contact, the floor, one-instrument caution (Vell).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md-27-- **Two falls to Lira** because the read is a beat late. "Say the rest of it out loud instead of writing it in the book where I have to wait for it." "You're the only person I've ever met who'd file a bruise."
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-55-  - **The Ember fragment.** ACQUIRED in the Karis match's third exchange (the edition's ch36, Thursday of week 16), with the notice P1 verbatim. It was lit once at the moment of taking. The *letting-go* is the second rewording; **"decision point" stays reserved for this book's ch21**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-56-  - **The entry-ledger mismatch.** Where this book's entry ledger says "B3 Ch13 … destabilization at about 18 hours, two misfires, settled in 11 days", reconcile to the edition: dawn misfires the day after the match, then Karis's two days, then the clean days (Book 3 ledger, wk16–17). Do not restate figures the edition does not give.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-57-  - **Karis and the Power Log.** Karis asked to read the Power Log at the end of Book 3 (ch60). She is one of "three people who know all of it". Before asking, she had never seen the binder.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-58-  - **Box seven.** Nine volumes went out, eight were shelved, and the gap is on Prynn's shelf. That is the plant; do not resolve it unless this book's map stages it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:59:  - **New canon from Book 3's repair:** Cael promised to write to Vell; Vell will teach him to read a ledger; Havel trained as a recorder after his "new grade".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-60-  - **Registry name and number:** "Caelen Hesk-ward, 41-7843-V". `[SHATTERED]` takes brackets only in documents read verbatim; spoken, it is plain *shattered*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-61-  - **Pronunciations (owner-confirmed):** Cael = KAYL; Lira = LEER-a.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-62-- **Courier calendar (edition canon).** Ilsev's query went down the hill Wednesday evening and returned Saturday after the fifth bell, and the referral went up Monday. **Book 4's "in the second hour of a review"** and the referral text's "of the preceding year" (B4 ch18) are known conflicts flagged by Book 3's review. When this book references the referral, use the courier timing and leave the year phrase out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md-63-- **Method.** Draft from your own event list, not from the source page (EDITION_BRIEF). Keep narration joined from the first draft: ≥40-word share 2.5–4.5%, and dialogue tags lean (drop "said" where the speaker is clear).
--
