editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-18-## What this movement is for
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-19-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-20-Four days, four measured rooms. Each tests a learned capability under changed conditions, and each costs a body. Turns and promises:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-21-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:22:- **Lira (cutaway, Ch51):** dawn, a hip that sets in two stages, Fenmark's hall in memory, and the north door. She cannot plan for his number and he cannot plan for hers; that was the point of nine days' silence. **Havel (cutaway):** a records officer off duty with nothing in his hands, choosing to be here.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-23-- **The Copper final (developed; the series' best-matched bout since Cael–Brom).** Two clocks: Brom's hardening fades past about four minutes, and Lira has three bursts with the fourth "the one she told him about." **1:** she asks the seam three ways and the counter is *already there*; it isn't speed but a different skeleton. She grins. **2:** Brom takes it; Rooke taught him to *stop finishing the absorption*, eating a fifth of every strike; two bursts; she is put on the boards. **3 (four minutes eleven):** the least Lira-shaped thing she has ever done — walking backward around the floor twice on foot, *spending his clock*; the stretch to five beats; the third burst; heel behind the knee. **4 (eleven seconds):** he goes straight at the hip, no disguise. The fourth burst. She lands on the bad hip *on purpose* so the fold carries her during a beat that can't move. "She used a wound as a mechanism." He hauls her up; neither lets go for three seconds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-24-- **The ceremony.** Withrow says the formula and nothing more. Bracken reads the certified record; **use the true win count (C6)**. **Fiske applauds first.** "She held it like an exhibit." One second's look at the delegation row.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-25-- **Ilsev (cutaway, Ch52):** reading the yard as text; Gault's filing read aloud; her two questions ("before or after"; "by a member of the panel or by a clerk"); "no objection to note, and I will record that I was present." Cael watches a lever work. The floor at the eighth bell: "Two years I've been trying to solve you." / "And?" / "Third one someday." **Vastin writes one line; the reader does not see it.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-26-- **Calibration night.** It takes twenty minutes to get Lira up the stairs ("Once. The first three times I did it to it by accident."). Karis's band, with the arithmetic checked by Bracken blind. **Brom: "Let it cost you… Like somebody with something in his pocket."** The rehearsal: run three is "weight five" because he stopped holding in the yard and the read came open, so on the day he will be on the stub (weight four at five of six, the bottom of the band). Trial four's regression trap: "land on the number." "A logged interval is a line in a record. A drift is evidence." **Lira's mechanism for the gaps:** eleven drifts counted, all in gaps; run the compound gaze, *his own*, on one person; "it's the only thing in the whole of your ledger that didn't come off somebody else." "Be the fighter. In a measured room. Both." **The slip**, inside the returned coursework folder: learned in a minute, burned in four seconds. Karis starts a question and stops herself: "No. Never mind." The Ember surprise is chosen and placed second. Log: "He wishes me *measured*… Sleep. Fight in the morning."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:27:- **The evaluation, the twentieth (two chapters).** Holding from the fourth hour; Brom on the stair ("I'll know. That's the best I've got."); Lira at the wing gate ("Say it if it goes."). Four chairs on the east wall; **Vastin has nothing in his hands**; Havel's four-tenths-of-a-second greeting. Gault restates the three points and asks for any addition: "The ignition point… Second." **1:** displacement eight times; the ceiling restated at *six*, "That is what the provision is for." **2:** the thermal vessel, four instants, "a better instrument reading than the Greyvane exhibit supports"; counsel and Ilsev find their one thing; Vastin does not write. **The drift at ninety minutes**, inside an honest answer: "Magister. I need an interval." Logged, "fatigue affecting response quality." **3:** the combined trial, eleven of twelve. **4:** the plate, Pressure-adjacent withheld (C9); a flat line that Gault defends ("That is what a real semester looks like"). **5: the second detent fails** off the upper rack, early and heavier. He takes a quarter of the burst and *shuts it mid-payment*, once, unrepeatable; the load goes into the hip; "Because the clerk was standing where I'd have landed." Void; the reserve frame; eleven minutes on the rail. The thin second. **Vastin does not look twice.** Eight of nine on the re-run, the last two degraded and said aloud. **6:** cold reprise. **The note, verbatim. Renewed.** Vastin rises last; the notebook has come out twice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-28-- **The log that night:** six hours of holding; two drifts; "Answer, on the twentieth of Reaping: yes."; "I'm going to stop calling it a habit"; "He didn't look twice… This is the first room I have ever been in with somebody who was simply finished."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-29-- **The interview, the twenty-first.** Bracken's subsection eleven, his own clerk secured with a written objection, the twelve-by-fourteen room. Prep: no page; **refuse in the open rather than hand over a true sentence with a hole in it**, because a hole tells the best reader *where*. "That's a good reason. It's also convenient." "Don't be clever." Eleven questions: the weakest element is the landing beat ("Lira has done it eleven times"); "can you do it again?" "No"; "A circuit. And everyone who beat me."; Prynn and Vell; "Why concede the category?"; **"So I can't lie to myself later."** The twelfth question is not asked. "I have never once in my life been in a room with somebody who could have taken something and didn't." The question back and the keynote, verbatim. The clerk's ruled column praised. Gault: "the most competent half-hour I have sat through in eleven years, and I did not say one word in it."
