editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-12.md:145:He walked back to his mark with the calf telling him about itself at every step, and knew that he had just bought the fifth exchange of the bout, deliberately, at the price of a leg. It was the doctrine's tax. He had paid it at the door, the way you pay a toll, so that the road beyond would go where he wanted it to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-12.md-146-
