editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-12.md-167-The yard-master stood where he was, blinking, and turned his head slowly and looked up at the slot in the gable where the beam ran out. He looked at it for a long time. Then he looked down at the bright bar on the floor at his feet. Cael saw him understand it, and saw what it cost him to understand it, after twenty years on these boards.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-12.md-168-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-12.md-169-He did not complain; he walked back to his mark.
