editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-49.md-159-Not to the lane. The lane was hers and she knew it the way she knew her own hand. She had laid it along the barrier because the barrier was the longest straight line on the floor and nobody on either side was using it, and she had gone down it, and the floor had become hers. Four of them had been where it closed, one after another. She had meant them to be.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-49.md-160-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-49.md:161:The fifth had not been.
