editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-49.md-163-He had been out in the middle near the round of old oak, and she had laid the lane at him, and when it closed he had been two steps to one side of it. Not a burst. Two steps on his own feet, taken before the lane came. Nobody had ever been early on one of her lanes. The file could not tell her how he had done it and she found she did not want to guess. Guessing was what people had done to her all her life.
