editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-52.md-95-Cael had been waiting for it since the first backward step, with his own count running silently under everything else. After every committed strike Brom re-squared his feet before the next. All season that had taken him four counts. Now, with the glass more than half gone, it took him five.
