editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-52.md-141-That beat was the Wind's one fixed price, half a breath of being locked upright and unable to turn. Cael had built his entire log round it. It had never been shortened by anyone, not by her and not by him, and Brom had known about it for two years. He turned into it and was waiting for her.
