editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-52.md-149-She did not cheat the beat. Nobody could, and she did not try. She let it run its whole length. What she chose, before she ever left the floor, was where she would come down, and she came down on the bad hip.
