editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-02.md-154-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-02.md-155-"The panel travels," he said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-02.md-156-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-02.md-157-Cael waited.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-02.md-158-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-02.md:159:"Your next evaluation. The provision's second." Gault tipped his head at the calendar behind him, where a line in his own hand marked the half-month and read *Panel of record: Gault, with two. Measured against: baseline (entry), and the note of the twentieth of Reaping.* "It falls inside the qualifying season. Under the old reading of the provision you'd have had to come home for it, wherever the season had taken you, and sit it here, in this wing, on this frame. The chancellor didn't care for that. She wrote to the registry's district office. The district office, to the astonishment of everybody who has ever written to a district office, agreed by return without a hearing." He unlaced his fingers to count on them. "The enrollment basis goes where the enrollee goes. The evaluation goes where the basis goes. So the evaluation goes where you go. If the delegation is in a mill town on the day, then the panel sits in the mill town."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-02.md-160-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-02.md-161-"With the same instruments?"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-02.md-162-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-02.md-163-"With instruments to the same standard, checked by me on the day, the way I check these on Fourth-days." Gault's face did something that in another man would have been a grin. "I have been issued a case. For the seals and the record books and the calibration weights. It is a very solid case." He paused. "It has a handle."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-02.md-164-
--
