editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-26.md-13-"Fourteen," she said round the pin, without turning. "Fourteen delegations, and I have thirteen. The fourteenth is a lake house that qualified at the year's turn on a recount, and nobody's printed anything about it yet. I've written to their registrar. Bracken says he'll answer, because registrars always answer registrars' friends." She took the pin out and stuck it in a slip. "Look."
