editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-11.md:73:"Stand there," she said, and pointed with one still finger at a place on the stone a pace and a half from the fifth-year. "Do not move from it. Do not put out a hand. If you feel anything you want to tell me about, tell me afterward, not during." She turned to the girl. "Three points. Quarter speed. Count it so he can follow."
