editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-51.md:89:Today the second-years had done a different sum. They had come an hour early with bread in their coat pockets and climbed to the back, because a full yard would shut the late half of the bluff out in the covered walk, and the back rows were the ones nobody could take from you.
