editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-51.md-123-With the fourth bell came Fiske, in plain clothes, to take a front-row seat on the north tier. Lira had told her to sit north, because from the east you could not see the far chalk properly, and Fiske had taken the advice as seriously as she took everything.
