editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-51.md:125:Two years the Copper Crown had sat on her shelf. Within the hour somebody else would be holding it in front of the whole bluff. She sat down in the front row with her hands loose in her lap and the face of a woman who had made her peace with that a long time ago, perhaps on the very afternoon she won it.
