editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-46.md:21:Nine feet out, Havel's near shoulder dropped and came forward.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-46.md-22-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-46.md:23:It did not come far. It came an inch, perhaps a little more, and it stayed there, and the whole of Havel's near side went with it, so that the stream he walked in narrowed by that much against the wall. They passed. For a moment Cael had, between his own sleeve and the records officer's case, a hand's breadth of air he had not had a moment before, in a walk where nobody had a hand's breadth of anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-46.md-24-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-46.md-25-Then the man was behind him, and the shoulder was level again, and the stream closed up.
