editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-46.md:159:A breath later the Force girl slid off low and touched the Stone boy on the knee again, very lightly, and the table called it hers. Two each. The bout went to a fifth, which the Stone boy won by rooting on the word and simply refusing to be moved until the girl ran out of ideas, and the tiers cheered him for it, which was fair; it had been clever. He would hold the fifth line into next year.
