editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-25.md:21:The notebook had a cardboard cover, soft at the corners, and ninety pages, and four of them had been written on. Between postings it lived in the locked drawer of his desk, under the spare blotters. On postings it lived in the inside pocket of his coat, over his heart, where his hand could find it without anybody seeing his hand move. Those were the only two places it had lived since a cold morning at Ardenmere, and it had never once lived anywhere else.
