editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-25.md:45:He pinned the sheet to the board in the long upper room over the Blade hall, where the squad had met at the beginning of the year. It was cold up there now, and the tall windows down one side were white with frost to the height of a man's head, and the lamps had been lit at the seventh bell because the day had not properly come. The five of them stood in front of the board in their coats with the two reserves behind them, and read it.
