editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-25.md:79:"Good. You'll learn the trial rules when Norhold prints them. They don't send them before the orientation; they never have. Until then you'll learn the floor." Rooke tapped the fifth line. "The squad is five. Four of you are certain. The fifth place is his, until a clerk at Norhold tells me otherwise. The Shield reserve learns the fifth place too, every drill, in case a clerk does." He looked at the Shield reserve, who had gone pale. "You'll travel. You'll want to be ready."
