editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-58.md:155:"The keeper of this room," he said, "can tell you how wrong each of these is. To the half minute. He doesn't throw them out for it. He knows each one's error, and he corrects for it, and so between them they tell him the time very well." He brought his eyes back. "That has been my work for forty years. Not finding the instrument that is right. Learning exactly how each one is wrong."
