editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-44.md:59:At Cael's left the counsel's pen moved. She had her privileged minute open in front of her, and across the top of the page, in her small capitals, written before any of them sat down, stood three headings. *RENEWALS. NINE DAYS. EVALUATOR.* She drew a line through the first.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-41.md:1:# Chapter 41 — The Empty Hill
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-41.md:9:At the top the house was emptying: the outer court was full of carts, and the lodge-man stood at his window with the arrivals book turned to its other face, the departures, writing a name for every trunk that went under the arch. Third-years shouted to one another across the flags about the next term as if it were a country. Somebody had left a cracked practice lath leaning against the capped well with a paper on it that said *FREE*, and nobody had taken it.
