+# CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES
+
+Scope: one sentence-level consolidation in chapter 44. No second author repair is warranted. All other repair-brief items are resolved; continuity, calendar, source distance, gates, and listening proof pass.
+
+This is a targeted informed recheck by the review seat, not a self-review, blind cold read, or real audience test. I read the full current movement, chapters 41–47, in order and checked the repair against `pre-repair/` with `diff -U0`.
+
+## (1) Brief items
+
+1. **RESOLVED — chapter 41 resident count.** The diff replaces “perhaps forty” with “forty-one,” “Four of the forty” with “Four of the forty-one,” and both refectory instances of “forty” with “forty-one.” The current text agrees in every exact census: “by dusk forty-one of them were left,” “all forty-one of the house's remaining enrollees,” “The forty-one sat close together,” and Bracken's “In residence: forty-one enrolled, by slip.”
+
+2. **RESOLVED — chapter 42 door approaches.** The diff replaces “five people” with “four young people”: “He had been told that four young people from the hill would come walking up to his door, one at a time.” The performed sequence is still exactly four—Lira, Karis, Cael, Brom—with Brom last. Seln supervises; “Five people in an orchard” and the five beans correctly count Seln with the four trainees.
+
+3. **RESOLVED — chapter 41 orientation.** The diff adds only the requested local bearings. Cael stays because leaving would be “entered as fled, with a note on three friends' files”; the concrete personal risk is “his enrollment struck out, and after it, a letter at a time, everything else with his name on it”; and “Six now” is grounded as “Six people now knew what was in the case on Karis's shelf.” The addition neither recaps Movement 6's discovery nor says what the case contains: “What it was, Cael did not write.” The five deniable routes, empty hill, and three-line Log entry are unchanged.
+
+4. **PARTIAL — chapter 44, Havel.** The repair correctly cuts two receipt-mechanics sentences and adds the needed causal answer: “The schedule did not give one. It gave the title, in a clerk's fair copy, and no office after it, on the old leaf or the new.” It also keeps the first sheet as the prior record, keeps six sheets and no seventh, and preserves *until relieved*. The residual is one local repetition: Havel's hope is stated first as the mark having to “say whose it was” and immediately again as wanting “the name of an office.” The coordinator called for one statement of that hope. Exact line fix 1 consolidates the two statements. The phrase “all these years” is not itself a continuity error: Book 4 establishes the pump-step origin, three entries written over two years, and two promotions since; Book 5 adds the fifth sheet at Norhold; Book 6 adds the sixth. The proposed consolidation removes the phrase incidentally rather than correcting its chronology.
+
+5. **RESOLVED — chapter 47 compression and ending.** The diff removes the abstract recap of the nine days, Gault's notes, the ninety-one, and the year of waiting half a beat early. It replaces the distributed cost recap with one concrete sentence: “It had cost what it cost: thirty slips for a room Karis might not be let speak in, a thousand landings on one foot, a letter on a table that could not be opened, a bundle as thick as a man's hand, ink to the knuckle.” The stronger inventory remains: “three boxes on a shelf, and two under a bed, and a carter's book in a coat, and a new strap on a satchel, and five beans in a gardener's jar.” The chapter still closes on “Next: Ostrand. Two sittings and a ruling.” followed by the bell and two new coats coming down to relieve the watchers.
+
+6. **RESOLVED — bounded cadence pass.** The diff shows the requested joins only in expository bridges in chapters 41, 44, 46, and 47. Representative repairs include “Withrow had gone ahead to her carriage and bowed to nobody, and Bracken was at the coach door with the seal,” “The protocol was sound still; he could find nothing wrong with any sentence of it,” and the joined opening of the eleventh sitting. Dialogue, short landing beats, Lira's bouts, the night spar, and the road-craft remain untouched. The share at or above forty words remains 4.4%, within the brief's 4.5% ceiling.
+
+### Repair-only source distance
+
+**Pass: 0 tracked passages.** I checked the changed joins and the new chapter 41 and chapter 44 sentences against source chapters 09, 14, 16, 18, 19, 20, and 22. The additions use plan-required facts—the *fled* default, the pending frame, Havel's known mark and office gap—but do not retain a source sentence's substantive beat order or wording. The post-repair sweep is 1% skeleton / 16% close over 1,474 sentences; none of its displayed skeleton pairs is a repair-added sentence. The displayed pairs remain generic false positives such as “She got up, with her hand on the buttress” versus “She set her hand flat on the face-down papers.” Exact overlap is 0 unprotected and 0 protected.
+
+## (2) Continuity
+
+- **Previous-movement join:** clean. Movement 6 ends with Vastin leaving the borrowed Ostrand room on day 98 after reading the case; chapter 41 returns the six separately to the bluff that evening and says only that the sixth knower is a Compact officer. It neither repeats the cache's findings nor gives the proceeding knowledge it does not have.
+- **Binding calendar:** pass. The `plan-audit.md` calendar remains intact: recess days 99–112; sittings six through eleven on days 117, 124, 138, 145, 152, and 166; envelope moved on day 173; last month opens day 176; closings days 187 and 194; ruling and Brom's panel day 201. `diff -U0` shows no repair edit that moves or renames a date. The only new date reference is the already-canon petition “Since the year's eighth day.”
+- **Counts:** forty-one resident enrollees everywhere in chapter 41; four trainees and four door approaches in chapter 42; five bodies in Seln's road arithmetic without taking the Movement 8 vote; eleven merits sittings plus two closings plus one ruling for Bracken's fourteen.
+- **Bodies and power:** Lira's right ankle is physically sound before the learned left-landing habit is corrected; Brom's left shoulder returns under load; Cael carries the priced spar and final-bout costs. Anchor remains idle and is quieted by naming; Shadow remains sealed; the public band never exceeds its ceiling. The private full-rate spar is known only to Lira and logs costs, not exchanges.
+- **Knowledge and reserved truths:** the cache remains known to exactly six and is not filed, published, described, or used. Havel and Ilsev remain unknowing; Havel stops at six sheets. Vastin performs only the one-line declination. No new `[UNBOUND]`, maker, Quieting, Architect, or Tide-practitioner material appears. There is no third off-channel action.
+- **Havel:** schedule two's fourteenth line gives the designation's title and no office on either leaf; his first sheet already records the mark's lack of an office. Six sheets remain between the second and third manuals; no seventh is written; *until relieved* plants the Movement 8 transfer request. “All these years” does not contradict Books 4–5, although line fix 1 removes the duplicated formulation around it.
+- **Velmere envelope:** chapter 47's single envelope is the day-45 letter carried for eighteen weeks, moved from Brom's left pocket to his table on day 173, twenty-eight days before the ruling. “The seal had not been broken.” No new envelope arrives.
+- **Ending and later-book inheritance:** nobody leaves, resigns, or votes. Three boxes are roped and deposited but unmentioned. The movement ends on “Next: Ostrand. Two sittings and a ruling.” and the changing of the coats. Movement 8 still owns the two closings, protected certification minute, ruling, council, vote, and public lid-off bout.
+- **Protected wording:** no Tier A or Tier B line is due in chapters 41–47. The Movement 8 certification minute is not prematurely quoted. The current one-line refusal—*The Archmarshal declines to certify.*—is the correct underlying act and does not relabel Vastin as Halcenvane's evaluator of record.
