+- **Chapter 42:** pass. Four approaches are promised and four are heard. The gardener, Seln, Lira, Karis, Cael, and Brom remain distinguishable in the six-person kitchen scene; “the fifth” consistently refers to the rotating sleeper. No numeric or abbreviation hazard.
+- **Chapter 43:** pass. Current/Force/Stone/Wind are capitalized role or Path terms whose surrounding syntax disambiguates them from common nouns. Fight calls, flags, feet, and speakers remain clear. The all-capital notebook headings are ordinary words, not spell-out acronyms.
+- **Chapter 44:** pass mechanically. Receipt, schedule, leaf, mark, title, and office remain distinct by ear. The proposed line fix is for duplicated reader explanation, not a quote, italics, or narrator-format fault. The repaired joins have clear subjects and no comma splice.
+- **Chapter 45:** pass. The board line “Wind, 28. Blade, 26.” is naturally voiced as two score labels. Blade/edge/line and left/right-foot sequences are physically clear; dialogue attribution in the private spar is stable. No broken join.
+- **Chapter 46:** pass. “Evaluator of record” consistently denotes Gault, while “Archmarshal” denotes Vastin. The five cadence joins retain explicit subjects. The five-word declination and the final tray sequence are clean aloud.
+- **Chapter 47:** pass. The joined eleventh-sitting opening remains grammatical. “The same day,” “Four weeks,” and “less a few days” have recoverable referents. The envelope, boxes, Log deletion, “Next: Ostrand,” and the final relief of the coats are distinct and correctly ordered. No unresolved ear collision.
